    "q-99775": {
      "dom_id": "step-q99775",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14220062/assets/929706c015fd38e83c9529a28203584a4e3e53a204ac3b4d20539d090a3fd25a.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y={12}^{x}+c.$ Determine the value of $c$ and find the equation of the curve.",
      "worked_solution": "The horizontal asymptote of $y={2}^{x}$ is $y=0.$ The vertical translation $y={12}^{x}+c$ shifts the asymptote to $y=c.$\n\nIn the graph above, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-3.$ Therefore, $c=-3.$",
