      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14220062/assets/d80c45f952e4c8a65349be524849104b1a76e6ee276186646c6c3facd83c8181.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the curve $y={7}^{x}+c.$ Determine the value of $c$ and find the equation of the curve.",
      "worked_solution": "The horizontal asymptote of $y={7}^{x}$ is $y=0.$ The vertical translation $y={7}^{x}+c$ shifts the asymptote to $y=c.$\n\nIn the graph above, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-5.$ Therefore, $c=-5.$",
